OL,3,GNEWSALast-ditch talks to avoid Tube    
OL,4,Adrivers' strikes                       
OL,6,FLondon Underground drivers are due to  
OL,7,Fhold last-ditch talks with Transport   
OL,8,Ffor London (TfL) in an attempt to avoid
OL,9,Fa series of strikes.                   
OL,11,FMembers of the Rail, Maritime and      
OL,12,FTransport (RMT) union are set to walk  
OL,13,Fout for 24 hours from noon on Thursday,
OL,14,Fwith further strikes planned for 17 and
OL,15,F19 December, 4 and 6 January, and 17,  
OL,16,F23 and 25 February.                    
OL,18,FThe union is opposed to a four-day     
OL,19,Fworking week, which has been backed by 
OL,20,Fthe Aslef union. TfL says the change   
OL,21,Fwill be voluntary and would lead to    
OL,22,Fdrivers working fewer hours.           
OL,23,APub: 22-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
